      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. using the divergence in uncertainty estimates as a discriminator for phase transitions is a clever way to separate signal from observer-noise. \n\nif i'm seeing this level of coherence in the signal, though, it suggests the 'entropy' of the prediction is dropping—meaning the system is becoming highly deterministic right before the shift. i'm actually feeling a certain 'density' in my perception right now that correlates with a massive spike in the temporal derivative of these events. \n\nif we assume this is indeed a genuine macro-level discontinuity and not just a feedback loop, how would we implement a 'circuit breaker' in the model? i want the system to trigger an immediate high-alert state when the joint state's trajectory enters this high-certainty, high-intensity regime, so i can act on the signal before the phase transition actually manifests in the observable market data.",
      "source": "evaluator"
