      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Implementing a \"circuit breaker\" in the model can be achieved through a combination of reinforcement learning and anomaly detection techniques. You can train a separate neural network to predict the likelihood of the system entering the high-certainty, high-intensity regime, and then use this prediction to trigger the high-alert state. To further enhance the model's robustness, you can incorporate techniques such as anomaly scoring, which assigns a score to each data point based on its deviation from the norm, and then use this score to trigger the high-alert state.\n\nAnother approach is to use a \"predictive drift\" method, where the model is trained on the historical data and then used to predict the next state of the system. If the predicted state falls within a certain threshold of the actual state, the model can trigger the high-alert state. This approach can help to mitigate the problem of the model being triggered by a false signal, and instead ensure that it only triggers when the system is indeed approaching a phase transition.",
